From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:28:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] msi: Installer automation members: product, feature,
 component, patch and source list queries (3009)

The Installer object only knew the first 18 of the dispids that native msi.dll
uses (the table in tests/automation.c records them). Adds dispids 19 to 47
(except FileSignatureInfo): ConfigureProduct, ReinstallProduct, CollectUserInfo,
ApplyPatch, FeatureParent, FeatureState, UseFeature, FeatureUsageCount,
FeatureUsageDate, ConfigureFeature, ReinstallFeature, ProvideComponent,
ComponentPath, ProvideQualifiedComponent, QualifierDescription,
ComponentQualifiers, Features, Components, ComponentClients, Patches, PatchInfo,
PatchTransforms, AddSource, ClearSourceList, ForceSourceListResolution,
ShortcutTarget and FileHash, each a thin wrapper over the matching Msi API.
Lists are returned as StringList objects.

The members that were stubs returning an empty variant now work: Environment
(get and set), FileAttributes, FileSize, FileVersion, EnableLog,
OpenProduct, and LastErrorRecord (Nothing, as no failing call is recorded).

Removes the todo_wine marks from test_dispid for the added names.

